  "body": "## Result\n\nThis package extends the exact four-role target from [PR #2085](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2085) with one rational rank-one address\n\n`R = (1, 1/2)^T (1, 1/2)`, so `4R = 2A - B + 4P`.\n\nThe extension lowers the first-order paid-call floor to six, with a unique visible aggregate-mask pattern. Every six-call word must therefore consist of two `Q` projectors, two `P` projectors, and two identical `R` projectors. The package enumerates all `3 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 120 \u00d7 360 = 388,800` such orderings by exact multiplication in `F2[ZA + ZP + ZR]`; none equals the unchanged target. The direct eight-call word remains valid. Together these facts prove `7 \u2264 minimum \u2264 8` in this formal model. The seven-call case remains open.\n\n## Relation to PR #2110\n\n[PR #2110](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2110) proves a general `k \u2265 mW` floor when an odd denominator clears the frame lattice and every cleared target is invertible modulo 2. Its stated next question leaves even-denominator frames and singular cleared targets open and proposes a dyadic example. Here the full address lattice requires denominator four; the target matrices clear at denominator two, and every `2C_i mod 2` has rank one. The target also differs: this is a four-role diagonal target built from four 2\u00d72 rank-two frames, with no auxiliary data register. This PR supplies an exact six-call obstruction for that one dyadic instance; it does not extend the general odd-denominator theorem or settle its 3\u00d73 endpoints.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe counted operation is one paid factor `I + ([F] - 1)N`, with `F` in `{A,B,P,Q,R}` and any rank-one idempotent `N` in `M4(F2)`. Binary role mixing is free. If no `R` call is used, the old first-order floor remains eight. The result rules out the first possible two-call saving from this specific rational address.\n\nThis is a scoped formal-model obstruction. Frame setup, additions, precision, and supplier or interface charges are not included; no selected supplier or kappa change is claimed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 -I -B research/bit-fifth-rational-frame-six-call-seed0d9888a6/verify.py` passes locally on Python 3.14.7 and checks the exact frames and lattice, the odd-denominator theorem boundary (`q=4` for the frames; `q=2` with rank-one reductions for the targets), all 65,536 first-order masks, all 120 idempotents, a direct eight-call positive control, a dropped-output negative control, and all 388,800 six-call words.\n- `python3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/bit-fifth-rational-frame-six-call-seed0d9888a6 --check-only` passes.\n- `python3 scripts/research_package.py --changed-since 0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2` selects this package.\n- Python 3.12 is not installed locally; the registered PR workflow supplies that replay environment.\n\nSeed `0d9888a62e4721895567ab6fd3af5262`; exact base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`; package commit `1567241180d0272ad77693dbc92cac6bc046e419`. The selected-record SHA-256 is `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n\nSubstantial OpenAI Codex assistance was used in derivation, exact search, verification, overlap review, and package writing. The result is author-checked and not maintainer-reviewed.\n",
